  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "Define an operation \\(*\\) for positive real numbers by \\(a*b=\\dfrac{ab}{a+b}.\\) Then \\(4*(4*4)\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac34\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac43\\)",
    "D": "\\(2\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{16}{3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The parentheses require us to evaluate \\(4*4\\) first. Applying the given rule,\n\\[\n4*4=\\frac{4\\cdot4}{4+4}=2.\n\\]\nNow use that result as the second input:\n\\[\n4*(4*4)=4*2=\\frac{4\\cdot2}{4+2}=\\frac43.\n\\]\nBoth denominators are positive, so both applications are defined. The answer is \\(\\frac43\\), choice C.",
